<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Clement VIII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1536">1536</a>–<a href="/years/1605">1605</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ippolito Aldobrandini</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Clement VIII reigned from 1592 to 1605. He absolved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry IV of France</a> in 1595 and brought the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> under direct papal rule in 1598, refusing to recognise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-d-este-duke-of-modena">Cesare d'Este</a> as heir. He also issued the Clementine Vulgate and raised small fiefs such as Masserano to principalities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-clement-viii.jpg" alt="Pope Clement VIII" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gelindu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1280282369_clement-viii.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
